.TH SM 5
.SH NAME
sm \- sheet metal part source
.SH DESCRIPTION
A part source for
.IR smfold (1)
has one statement per line; # begins a comment.
An argument is an expression without spaces, or one in parentheses:
numbers, names, + \- * /, the functions
floor tan sin cos sqrt max hypot atan2 (angles in degrees),
and the units in, mm and deg.
Lengths are in mm.
Flat coordinates are x and y; the sheet occupies z in [\-t, 0], and its
top face, z = 0, is the reference face.
Statements are applied in order.
.TP
.BI include " file"
Read
.I "name = expr"
lines from
.IR file ,
relative to this file.
.TP
.I "name = expr"
A local definition.
.TP
.BI sheet " t r k"
Thickness, inside bend radius, k-factor.
.TP
.BI plate " name x0 y0 x1 y1 " origin " ox oy oz " axes " u v"
The root slab.
Flat x and y run along the 3D axes
.I u
and
.I v
(+x, \-z, ...); the top face faces
.IR u " \(mu " v ,
and flat (0, 0) is at the origin.
.TP
.BI flange " name parent dir angle leg"
.RB [ at
.IR c ]
.RB [ span
.IR "a b" ]
.RB [ zone
.IR "a b" ]
.br
A bend zone, then a straight leg, on the edge of
.I parent
in flat direction
.I dir
(+x \-x +y \-y), or on the line where that coordinate is
.IR c .
A positive angle, in degrees, folds toward the top face.
.I Span
is the extent along the edge (default that of the parent);
.I zone
that of the bend (default the overlap of span and parent).
.TP
.BI cut " u0 v0 u1 v1 " along " a"
.RB [ at
.I w
.B depth
.IR l ]
.br
A rectangle cut through every slab so far that lies across the 3D axis
.I a
.RI ( u
and
.I v
are the other two axes, in alphabetical order),
or only to depth
.I l
about
.IR w .
.TP
.BI hole " d u v " along " a"
.RB [ at
.I w
.B depth
.IR l ]
.RB [ csink
.I dc angle
.BR near | far ]
.RB [ pattern
.I ax n p
.RI [ "ax n p" ]
|
.B pattern hex
.I p
.B within
.IR r ]
.br
A hole, as for a cut.
A pattern repeats it
.I n
times,
.I p
apart along the signed axis
.IR ax ;
a hex pattern fills the circle of radius
.I r
with a hexagonal grid.
A countersink is made at the top face (near) or the other (far).
.TP
.BI outline " along a"
.RB [ at
.I w
.B depth
.IR l ]
.br
.BI point " u v"
.RB [ arc
.I cu cv
.BR ccw | cw ]
.br
A hole of any outline, as for a cut, given by the points that follow,
each joined to the next by a line or an arc about
.RI ( cu ,
.IR cv ).
.TP
.BI trim " along a"
.RB [ at
.I w
.B depth
.IR l ]
.br
An open curve of points from the outline of a slab face to another
point of it; the smaller piece is cut off.
.TP
.BI round " name r"
.RB [ at
.IR "x y z" ]
.br
Round the two free corners of flange
.IR name ,
or the corner of slab
.I name
at the point (a round if convex, a fillet if concave).
.SH SEE ALSO
smfold(1), fold(5)
